    "title": "The Trans-Siberian Railway",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "The Trans-Siberian Railway is the longest railway line in the world. It runs for 9,289 kilometres from Moscow in the west to Vladivostok on the Pacific coast in the east. A complete journey takes about seven days and crosses eight time zones."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Construction began in 1891 and took twenty-five years. Thousands of workers built the line across forests, mountains and frozen ground, often in temperatures far below zero. The railway was designed to connect the distant east of Russia to Moscow and to help the country develop its economy. Before it opened, a journey from Moscow to the Pacific could take months."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Today, there are three classes of tickets. In first class, two passengers share a small bedroom. In second class, four passengers share a compartment with bunk beds. The cheapest option, third class, has open carriages with sixty beds. Each carriage has a hot-water boiler, so passengers can make tea and instant noodles at any time. A dining car serves hot meals, but many travellers prefer to buy food from local people who sell it on the platforms."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Most visitors break the journey in several cities. Popular stops include Yekaterinburg, near the border between Europe and Asia, and Irkutsk, close to Lake Baikal, the deepest lake in the world. Many travellers say the best part of the trip is meeting other passengers. With so many hours together, people play cards, share stories and sometimes make friends for life."
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "If you want to travel, book early. The most popular trains in summer are often full months before. Take warm clothes even in July, because the weather can change quickly. And most important, bring a good book and plenty of patience: after the first two days, even the most beautiful scenery starts to look familiar."
      }
    ]
  },
